{"title":"Square root","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>square root</b> of a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/a/7bab13715d74c8caa653a0f6524f08e3c2499986.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />. Generally, the square root only takes the positive value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. This can be altered by placing a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/2/91205e81c98c486418902c88d5c396f5355491f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> before the root.  Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is a square root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the square of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Notation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Notation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Exponential_notation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Exponential notation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Properties\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Properties</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notation\">Notation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_root&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Notation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The square root (or the principal square root) of a number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is denoted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aa027abf288d84604eb02f64f3b9485aa648ed7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />.  For instance, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/5/eb58d5528cef6e633dd5c25b21abe2ad719d50be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt 4 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />.  When we consider only <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_number\" title=\"Positive number\">positive</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">reals</a>, the square root <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function/Introduction&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Function/Introduction (page does not exist)\">inverse</a> of the squaring function. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Exponential_notation\">Exponential notation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_root&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Exponential notation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Square roots can also be written in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Exponentiation\" title=\"Exponentiation\">exponential</a> notation, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9cc353854c2985a85ba7767b86215a4c20f19d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{\\frac 12}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to the square root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.  Note that this agrees with all the laws of exponentiation, properly interpreted.  For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/7/917ce7a738972b250ea3c5af007d28c978f46ac4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(x^{\\frac12}\\right)^2 = x^{\\frac12 \\cdot 2} = x^1 = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"181\" height=\"35\" />, which is exactly what we would have expected.  This notion can also be extended to more general <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rational\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rational\">rational</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Real\">real</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Complex\">complex</a> powers, but some caution is warranted because these do not give functions.  In particular, if we require that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9cc353854c2985a85ba7767b86215a4c20f19d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^{\\frac 12}$\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /> always gives the positive square root of a positive real number, then the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/f/04fc322d0f79e34c15c66ef01e2c0f596f168f2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(x^2\\right)^{\\frac 12} = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"79\" height=\"28\" /> does not hold.  For example, replacing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on the left but gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> on the right.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties\">Properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_root&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>No square roots are negative. This is because the positive root is always taken.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square_root&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Algebra\" title=\"Algebra\">Algebra</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Root_(operation)\" title=\"Root (operation)\">Root (operation)</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Square_root&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018110950\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 131/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 274/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3671/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.327      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.327      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2588:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018110950 and revision id 242053. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}